A path that will not become a URL must read as nil, not raise.

dataWithContentsOfFile: reached initWithContentsOfURL: with whatever fileURLWithPath: returned, and
that method raises NSInvalidArgumentException on a nil url. fileURLWithPath: hands back nil for
input it will not accept, so a caller that only ever asked to read a file got an exception instead
of the nil every caller is written against. macOS returns nil from dataWithContentsOfFile: for
anything it cannot read.

The plain initWithContentsOfFile: already guarded a nil PATH. It did not guard a nil URL built from
a non nil path, and the options:error: form guarded neither. Both do now.

MEASURED, and it cost iTerm2 its entire Preferences window for as long as the port has existed.
ProfilesGeneralPreferencesViewController awakeFromNib calls updateImageWell, which builds an
NSImage from the profile background image path. With no background image configured that path is
the EMPTY STRING, fileURLWithPath: returns nil for it, and the raise walked out of awakeFromNib,
out of the nib load, out of -[NSWindowController window], and out of -[PreferencePanel run] before
run could reach its own code. The trace is exact:

  cider: RAISE NSInvalidArgumentException: cannot create data from nil url
  cider:   Foundation   -[NSData(NSData) initWithContentsOfURL:options:error:]
  cider:   Foundation   +[NSData(NSData) dataWithContentsOfFile:]
  cider:   AppKit       +[NSImageRep imageRepsWithContentsOfFile:]
  cider:   AppKit       -[NSImage initWithContentsOfFile:]
  cider:   iTerm2       -[ProfilesGeneralPreferencesViewController updateImageWell]
  cider:   iTerm2       -[ProfilesGeneralPreferencesViewController awakeFromNib]
  cider:   AppKit       -[NSNib instantiateNibWithExternalNameTable:]
  cider:   AppKit       -[NSWindowController loadWindow]
  cider:   AppKit       -[NSWindowController window]
  cider:   iTerm2       -[PreferencePanel window]
  cider:   iTerm2       -[PreferencePanel run]

Before: the panel nib prints loadNibFile enter and never loadNibFile leave, while three other
window controllers in the same run reach done. After: no raise in the run at all, and the awake
walk goes on past the object that used to end it into defineControl and updateEnabledState.

This also corrects the account this defect had been given for weeks. run was believed to bail on
"if ([[self window] isVisible]) return;" with isVisible answering true. It does not: with the two
event loop pollers filtered out, run asks the panel isVisible ZERO times, because the raise takes
it out before it gets there. The disassembly of run is right, the reading of the branch is right,
and run simply never arrives at it.

CIDER_TRACE_DATAFILE names a path that would not convert, which is how the empty string was found.

--- a/src/NSData.m
+++ b/src/NSData.m
@@ -850,7 +850,15 @@
 
 - (id)initWithContentsOfFile:(NSString *)path options:(NSDataReadingOptions)readOptionsMask error:(NSError **)errorPtr
 {
-    return [self initWithContentsOfURL:[NSURL fileURLWithPath:path] options:readOptionsMask error:errorPtr];
+    /* The same rule as the plain form above, which had the guard while this one did not. */
+    NSURL *url = (path == nil) ? nil : [NSURL fileURLWithPath:path];
+
+    if (url == nil)
+    {
+        [self release];
+        return nil;
+    }
+    return [self initWithContentsOfURL:url options:readOptionsMask error:errorPtr];
 }
 
 - (id)initWithContentsOfURL:(NSURL *)url options:(NSDataReadingOptions)readOptionsMask error:(NSError **)errorPtr
@@ -925,7 +933,34 @@
         [self release];
         return nil;
     }
-    return [self initWithContentsOfURL:[NSURL fileURLWithPath:path] options:0 error:NULL];
+    /*
+     * A PATH THAT WILL NOT BECOME A URL MUST READ AS nil, NOT RAISE.
+     *
+     * initWithContentsOfURL: raises on a nil url, and fileURLWithPath: hands back nil for inputs
+     * it will not accept, so a caller that only ever asked to read a file got an exception. macOS
+     * returns nil from dataWithContentsOfFile: for anything it cannot read, which is what callers
+     * are written against.
+     *
+     * This cost iTerm2 its whole Preferences window. ProfilesGeneralPreferencesViewController
+     * awakeFromNib calls updateImageWell, which builds an NSImage from the profile background
+     * image path; the raise unwound out of awakeFromNib, out of the nib load, out of
+     * -[NSWindowController window] and out of -[PreferencePanel run] before anything could be
+     * shown, and nothing reported it. See docs/iterm2-preferences-gap.md.
+     */
+    NSURL *url = [NSURL fileURLWithPath:path];
+
+    if (url == nil)
+    {
+        if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_DATAFILE") != NULL)
+        {
+            fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_DATA no url for path len=%u [%s]\n",
+                    (unsigned)[path length], [path UTF8String] ?: "(no utf8)");
+            fflush(stderr);
+        }
+        [self release];
+        return nil;
+    }
+    return [self initWithContentsOfURL:url options:0 error:NULL];
 }
 
 - (id)initWithContentsOfURL:(NSURL *)url
